B) The project is ahead of schedule, since it has already spent more than it planned to
C) The project is on track, since about half of the work has been done
D) The CPI is about 1.40, which shows good cost performance
= A
? CPI = EV / AC = 50% of BAC / 70% of BAC ≈ 0.71. Less than a dollar of value is earned for each dollar spent.

@@ PR9 | Agile
The sprint burndown stays flat for most of the sprint and then drops sharply on the last day. What does this suggest?
A) Stories are finished only at the end; the team should split work and finish items steadily
B) The team is working very efficiently, since all of the work is completed within the sprint
C) The burndown chart is broken and should be replaced with a different tool for the team
D) The product owner is adding new work each day, which keeps the burndown chart flat
= A
? A late drop suggests mini-waterfalls within the sprint. Smaller stories and finishing items one at a time improve flow and reduce risk.

@@ PR9 | Hybrid
Reports say that testing is 90% complete, but users report many failures in the test environment. What should the project manager do?
A) Inspect the actual test results and deliverables to verify the status
B) Accept the reported status, since the test lead prepared the report
C) Ask the users to stop reporting failures until testing is complete
D) Increase the reported figure to 95% to recognise the team's effort during testing
= A
? Status should be verified against evidence. Inspecting actual results and deliverables reveals the real situation.

@@ PR10 | Predictive
What must happen before the plant is handed back to operations after a shutdown?
A) Permits closed, temporary equipment removed and the pre-startup review done
B) The final invoices from all contractors received and paid in full by the plant
C) The lessons learned report approved by the sponsor and the plant's board
D) All of the contract workers demobilised and their accommodation closed
= A
? A safe handover requires that work is complete and verified, permits are closed and temporary equipment is removed. Commercial and lessons learned activities can follow.

@@ PR10 | Hybrid
The security programme is ending, but its controls must keep working. What should the closure include?
A) Transferring each control to a named operational owner, with procedures and metrics
B) Ask the programme team to keep running the controls informally after the programme has closed
C) Switching off the controls that do not yet have an owner in the organisation
D) Documenting the controls in the final report and leaving them as they are
= A
? Sustaining value after closure requires clear operational ownership, documented procedures and measures of performance.

@@ PR10 | Hybrid
At the end of a funded research project, the funder requires the data to be preserved and shared. What should the project do?
A) Deposit the data in an approved repository, as the data management plan requires
B) Keep the data on the lead researcher's laptop in case anyone asks for it
C) Delete the data, since the research questions have now been answered
D) Send the data by email to anyone who requests it, without any conditions or checks
= A
? Funders' data requirements are closure obligations. An approved repository preserves the data and makes it available under the agreed conditions.

@@ PR10 | Predictive
Under the vendor contract, the final payment is due on acceptance after the parallel run. What should be confirmed first?
A) That the acceptance criteria have been met
B) That the vendor has sent its final invoice for the work
C) That the users say they like the new system
D) That the project budget still has enough money left
= A
? Formal acceptance against the agreed criteria comes before final payment and contract closure.

@@ PR10 | Agile
At the end of the final sprint, two stories are unfinished. What happens to them?
A) They are not done, and they go back to the product backlog for the product owner
B) They are counted as done, since most of the work on them has been completed by the team
C) They are deleted, since the project has ended and nobody will work on them any more
D) They are moved into the sprint report as completed work with a note explaining the gaps
= A
? Only items that meet the definition of done count as complete. Unfinished items go back to the product backlog.

@@ PR10 | Predictive
As the shutdown ends, contractor crews finish their work at different times. What should the project manager do?
A) Demobilise crews as their work is accepted, checking tools, permits and badges
B) Keep all of the crews on site until the last crew has finished, so that they leave together
C) Let each crew leave whenever it wants, without checking its work or its equipment
D) Ask the crews to stay for an extra week in case the plant has problems after restart
= A
? Releasing resources as their work is accepted controls cost, while administrative checks close out access and equipment properly.
